From 527460ce103e512f3942f2679e19edd59c706a9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 09:44:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firewall UI: say when changes are pending, and stop calling
 "no exemption" any

Two defects from the owner's first hands-on with Service Intercept on v2.8.9.

1. THE EXEMPT COLUMN READ AS THE OPPOSITE OF THE TRUTH. An empty exemption
rendered through rfwDash(), whose placeholder is RFW_160 - literally the word
"any". In an Exempt column that says "everything is exempt"; it means "no
ADDITIONAL exemption". (It is correct in the Forwards Source column, which is
where it was copied from.) Now renders RFW_100 "None", which already exists in
all 25 dicts. Cosmetic only - the engine always exempted the target regardless
of this field, which is the exemption that actually matters.

2. NOTHING TOLD YOU AN EDIT WAS INACTIVE, OR WHERE APPLY WAS. Reported as "do
Zones and Forwards apply automatically? I don't see an apply button." They do
not: every tab writes to the draft via action=save, and the single "Apply and
confirm" - and the commit-confirm card with Keep/Revert - both live inside the
Rules tab. From Zones, Forwards or Service Intercept there was no apply control,
no indication the row was not in effect, and no pointer to where it was. A row
appearing in a table read as "live".

Added a page-level banner OUTSIDE the tab containers, so it shows from every
tab, with the two states kept distinct because conflating them would be worse
than silence:
  dirty && !armed -> saved to the draft, NOTHING is in effect yet
  armed           -> applied, waiting for Keep, reverts on its own if ignored
plus a "Go to Rules" button, since Apply/Keep/Revert genuinely live there.

`dirty` is a REAL signal from the engine, not a client-side guess: action=cfg
now reports whether any of the eight draft files exists. That is exactly the
right test - reaper_fw_list_get() resolves draft > lastgood > legacy nvram, and
the confirm path deletes the whole draft dir once consumed into lastgood
(reaper_fw.c:2733), so a leftover file can only mean unapplied or unconfirmed
work. Because it comes from the router it survives a page reload, which a
session flag would not; a save also sets it locally so the banner appears at
once rather than on the next poll.

3 tokens RFW_273-275 appended to all 25 dicts in lockstep (6765 -> 6768).

Verified: the dirty block extracted and compiled standalone under -Wall -Wextra,
then run against a fake draft dir - empty 0, draft/nat 1, draft/zone 1, dir
removed 0. Page: every new id resolves, all tokens resolve in EN.dict, the
inline block parses under node --check, div tags balance (173/173), ASCII-clean,
reaper_langcheck 0 breakers / 22 pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
